  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Tenuiphenone B may interact with CD70 antigen through multiple pathways. The first path indicates that Tenuiphenone B targets WiDr, which in turn is targeted by a compound that directly binds to CD70 antigen. The second and third paths show that Tenuiphenone B also targets DNA polymerase eta, which is subsequently targeted by another compound that also binds to CD70 antigen. These findings collectively imply that Tenuiphenone B may exert its effects through different molecular mechanisms, all leading to the interaction with CD70 antigen. The evidence is consistent with the possibility that Tenuiphenone B influences CD70 antigen through various intermediate targets, potentially modulating immune responses or other biological processes involving CD70. The strength of the evidence is moderate, as the scores are relatively similar across the different paths, but the exact mechanism by which Tenuiphenone B interacts with CD70 antigen remains uncertain, requiring further experimental validation.",
